rent removal) is the focus: R2.1 (remove parents successively), R2.2 (stop at non-empty parent), R2.3 (independent processing of multiple args)\n     - Non-goals: no non-empty removal, no file arguments, no stdin reading\n\n   - **cmd/rmdir/main.go** (existing, needs modification)\n     - Already has `options` struct with `parents`, `verbose`, `ignoreFailOnNonEmpty` booleans\n     - Already parses all flags (-p, --parents, -v, --verbose, --ignore-fail-on-non-empty, --help, --version)\n     - The `run` function currently ignores options (`_ options`) and only does basic `syscall.Rmdir`:\n     ```go\n     func run(_ options, dirs []string) int {\n         exitCode := 0\n         for _, dir := range dirs {\n             if err := syscall.Rmdir(dir); err != nil {\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"rmdir: failed to remove '%s': %s\\n\",\n                     dir, sysErrMsg(err))\n                 exitCode = 1\n             }\n         }\n         return exitCode\n     }\n     ```\n     - Has `sysErrMsg` helper mapping errno values to GNU-compatible error messages (ENOTEMPTY, ENOENT, ENOTDIR, EACCES)\n     - Has full arg parser with `parseArgs`, `parseLongFlag`, `parseShortFlags`\n\n   - **cmd/rmdir/rmdir_test.go** (existing, needs modification)\n     - Has `TestDiff` with subtests: no_args, nonexistent, not_a_directory, nonempty, single_empty, multiple_empty, partial_failure, multiple_nonexistent\n     - Uses both `testutils.RunDiffTests` and custom `runBin`/`compareResults` for tests that need per-binary filesystem setup\n     - `runRemovalTest` helper creates separate temp dirs for Go and ref binaries, runs both, compares results\n     - `normalizeBinaryName` regex: `(/\\S+/)?g?rmdir\\b` → replaces with \"rmdir\"\n     - `binResult` struct: `{stdout, stderr []byte; exitCode int}`\n     - `runBin` uses `context.WithTimeout(10s)`, sets `LC_ALL=C`, uses `errors.AsType[*exec.ExitError]`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. The task was in the re