{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01D4LuxkcgFhzNB97VZt129S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The divergence is in the error message format. GNU rmdir uses \"failed to remove directory 'a'\" (with \"directory\" included) when removing parent directories with `-p`, while my code uses \"failed to remove 'a'\" (without \"directory\").\n\nLooking at the ref stderr: `rmdir: failed to remove directory 'a': Directory not empty`\nAnd go stderr: `rmdir: failed to remove 'a': Directory not empty`\n\nSo when `-p` is used, GNU rmdir includes \"directory\" in the error message. Let me check if this is only for parent directories or for the initial target too.\n\n\nThe regular error format without `-p` is `\"rmdir: failed to remove 'dir': Error\"`, but when `-p` triggers a parent removal failure, GNU rmdir switches to `\"rmdir: failed to remove directory 'dir': Error\"`. I need to verify whether this \"directory\" keyword applies only to parent removals or also to the initial target when using `-p`. Updating the error message format for parent directory removals...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1018,"cache_read_input_tokens":40740,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1018},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f5387b89-d825-4661-8fb6-2f9ccc9b70c5","uuid":"ff0b733b-64bf-4df1-98b2-1e65c6744874"}
